                <pb facs="0703" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.111 Quota/338: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-13T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>185. Embassy’s 240, December 2, 2 p.m. The Department understands the importance
                    which Mussolini’s Government attaches to the subject of Italian immigration into
                    this country.</p>
                <pb facs="0704" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/>
                <p>The Department will keep you fully informed with respect to any representations
                    which the new Italian Ambassador may make on this question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
